# Guard, not a build configuration.
#
# The deployable app is the Next.js radar in web/, and the mechanism that
# selects it is the Vercel project's Root Directory setting (set it to `web`).
# See web/README.md.
#
# This file exists for the state where that setting is missing. With the repo
# root as the project root, Vercel scans it, finds pyproject.toml, and offers to
# deploy spy_der/app/api.py as a serverless FastAPI function. That must never
# happen: the app exposes unauthenticated mutating routes, including
# POST /risk/kill-switch?enabled=false, which would publish a public reset for a
# latched kill switch. It is also stateful by design — the pipeline carries the
# HMM belief, the flow and wall trackers and the open book — so a serverless
# runtime would discard all of it on every cold start, and the SQLite audit
# store cannot write outside /tmp.
#
# Keeping the engine out of the upload means that detection cannot fire even if
# the Root Directory setting is lost or a new project is imported at the root.
#
# The engine belongs on the dedicated CPU VPS behind loopback: deploy/CPU_VPS.md

spy_der/
scripts/
tests/
deploy/
docs/
pyproject.toml
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
*.db
.github/
